WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:05.069
Okay, let's dig into these new DNC debate
requirements.

00:00:05.069 --> 00:00:09.890
The Democratic Party has put in place some
new and stricter requirements to make the

00:00:09.890 --> 00:00:14.900
third and fourth officially DNC sanctioned
primary debates, which are scheduled to take

00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:19.680
place in a, we'll put it up on the screen
in a second, but I believe it's a September

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:23.630
and October is when debates three and four
will take place.

00:00:23.630 --> 00:00:27.690
And there's a lot to talk about here and I
want to sort of do this justice and really

00:00:27.690 --> 00:00:31.710
go through it piece by piece and think it
through because a lot of the reactions I've

00:00:31.710 --> 00:00:35.530
seen online to these requirements are not
making a lot of sense.

00:00:35.530 --> 00:00:37.280
So first let's zoom out a little bit.

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:39.190
Why do we have requirements?

00:00:39.190 --> 00:00:44.859
Why do we have minimum standards that need
to be met to participate in debates?

00:00:44.859 --> 00:00:51.440
Well, if you have no standards at all, you
can end up with dozens, 50 I mean you've got

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:57.789
to have some, you know, does anyone who announces
a candidacy get to participate in DNC sanctioned

00:00:57.789 --> 00:00:58.789
debates?

00:00:58.789 --> 00:01:02.949
There's anybody who's on the ballot in even
one state get to participate.

00:01:02.949 --> 00:01:07.150
It's chaos if you have no minimum requirements
whatsoever.

00:01:07.150 --> 00:01:13.390
But on the other side of this, we know 2016
being a prime example that the DNC has ways

00:01:13.390 --> 00:01:21.250
of influencing the Democratic primary that
can be anti progressive anti insurgent candidate

00:01:21.250 --> 00:01:25.200
and basically pro status quo, pro establishment
candidate.

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:31.260
And so what we don't want to have our requirements
that are so strict that they preempted the

00:01:31.260 --> 00:01:38.920
possibility of having serious insurgent progressive
candidates and challengers for the 2028 Democratic

00:01:38.920 --> 00:01:39.920
primary.

00:01:39.920 --> 00:01:43.180
So the first debates are in late June and
late July.

00:01:43.180 --> 00:01:44.180
We're very close.

00:01:44.180 --> 00:01:48.660
I mean we're a month from the first debate
and the requirements for those first two debates,

00:01:48.660 --> 00:01:53.850
which are going to be split into a and B,
uh, because the field is still so large.

00:01:53.850 --> 00:01:59.550
The requirement for those first two debates,
which will be debate one a and one B and debate

00:01:59.550 --> 00:02:01.270
two a and two B.

00:02:01.270 --> 00:02:03.160
We've known about these for a while.

00:02:03.160 --> 00:02:09.859
65,000 individual donors and you need to be
polling 1% in three qualified polls closer

00:02:09.859 --> 00:02:11.090
to the date of the debate.

00:02:11.090 --> 00:02:14.969
So the pope will look at the polls now have
to figure out who would be in as of today.

00:02:14.969 --> 00:02:18.670
Uh, but what's going to matter is how the
candidates are doing closer to the debates

00:02:18.670 --> 00:02:20.489
in mid to late June.

00:02:20.489 --> 00:02:23.120
So we'll put up on the screen for you.

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:25.709
Also the requirements for the following debates.

00:02:25.709 --> 00:02:33.219
So first two debates, 65 k donors and 1% in
three qualified polls.

00:02:33.219 --> 00:02:38.819
The DNC has now added stricter requirements
for debates three and four and debates three

00:02:38.819 --> 00:02:39.819
and four.

00:02:39.819 --> 00:02:44.499
The requirements double the donor number two,
130,000 donors.

00:02:44.499 --> 00:02:50.329
And they also double the polling requirement
to 2% instead of 1% and that needs to be in

00:02:50.329 --> 00:02:53.520
for rather than just three poles.

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:59.980
So the criticisms immediately from some people
have been, this is going to destroy the field.

00:02:59.980 --> 00:03:02.400
This is unfair to smaller candidates.

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:05.489
This is a establishment DNC move.

00:03:05.489 --> 00:03:12.139
This is potentially going to alienate donors
to those, uh, uh, lower ranked candidates

00:03:12.139 --> 00:03:16.340
because they will say, well, why am I even
going to bother if these new, even higher

00:03:16.340 --> 00:03:21.349
requirements are going to keep them out of
the third and forth debate anyway, we want

00:03:21.349 --> 00:03:25.249
the field to stay bigger for a longer period
of time.

00:03:25.249 --> 00:03:30.919
I think we have to break this down into two
parts, the donor requirement and the polling

00:03:30.919 --> 00:03:31.919
requirement.

00:03:31.919 --> 00:03:32.919
Okay.

00:03:32.919 --> 00:03:35.040
Let's first talk about the 2% polling requirement.

00:03:35.040 --> 00:03:39.359
Um, the DNC, uh, the convention is in, it's
in the summer.

00:03:39.359 --> 00:03:44.430
I don't know if it's scheduled for June, July,
or August, but it's in summer of 2020.

00:03:44.430 --> 00:03:51.829
If you don't have 2% by the third debate in
September, I believe it is completely reasonable

00:03:51.829 --> 00:03:56.400
to say you can't continue being in the officially
sanctioned DNC debates.

00:03:56.400 --> 00:04:04.480
If you can't get to 2% after two national
debates and six or seven months of campaigning

00:04:04.480 --> 00:04:08.870
for most of these candidates, you don't have
a shot and you are becoming a distraction

00:04:08.870 --> 00:04:14.689
period and you're taking time away from the
candidates who are in this thing, having time

00:04:14.689 --> 00:04:17.470
to better flesh out and talk about their ideas.

00:04:17.470 --> 00:04:23.160
I have no problem whatsoever with a 2% polling
requirement for the third and fourth debates.

00:04:23.160 --> 00:04:25.950
The question mark for me is a 130,000 donors.

00:04:25.950 --> 00:04:26.950
Okay.

00:04:26.950 --> 00:04:33.510
Bill share pointed out on Twitter that back
in 2008, John Edwards had like 20,000 donors

00:04:33.510 --> 00:04:37.350
or something like that at a relatively advanced
point in the campaign.

00:04:37.350 --> 00:04:40.700
He was a serious candidate in terms of the
polling.

00:04:40.700 --> 00:04:45.280
Um, but uh, he did not have a 130,000 donors.

00:04:45.280 --> 00:04:51.480
So I think that it's really important to point
out that if we want to make a case that these

00:04:51.480 --> 00:04:57.250
requirements are too strict, it's got to be
along the number of donors line.

00:04:57.250 --> 00:05:04.620
I don't think there is any serious case to
be made that 2% by a September is too high

00:05:04.620 --> 00:05:05.620
of a threshold.

00:05:05.620 --> 00:05:10.840
Now, let's understand a little bit about,
uh, what the effect would be of the 1% and

00:05:10.840 --> 00:05:14.400
2% polling requirements based on today's numbers.

00:05:14.400 --> 00:05:15.400
Okay.

00:05:15.400 --> 00:05:19.170
To be in the first debates, you need to pull
1%.

00:05:19.170 --> 00:05:23.880
If we look at the current average polling,
remember what matters is how they pull right

00:05:23.880 --> 00:05:24.950
before the debates.

00:05:24.950 --> 00:05:30.250
Not right now, but let's imagine that we had
today's polling as the sort of way to decide

00:05:30.250 --> 00:05:31.840
who gets into the debates.

00:05:31.840 --> 00:05:38.620
You have Bennet Bullock, Hickenlooper, Seth
Moulton, Bill de Blasio, Delaney, Kirsten

00:05:38.620 --> 00:05:42.560
Gillibrand, Marianne Williamson, Tim Ryan,
and Tulsi Gabard.

00:05:42.560 --> 00:05:44.100
That's 10 candidates.

00:05:44.100 --> 00:05:46.270
None of them are pulling 1% right now.

00:05:46.270 --> 00:05:47.270
Okay?

00:05:47.270 --> 00:05:53.390
There are uh, uh, or rather, I'm sorry, there
are 10 candidates who are polling 1% right

00:05:53.390 --> 00:05:58.190
now and that's still a very solid number for
the first and second debate.

00:05:58.190 --> 00:06:03.060
There is a broad range of opinion represented
among those 10 candidates.

00:06:03.060 --> 00:06:07.770
So there would be a bunch of people who would
be out today if the requirement, we're 1%

00:06:07.770 --> 00:06:10.100
but we would still have 10 people participating.

00:06:10.100 --> 00:06:12.280
Very reasonable for this early in the game.

00:06:12.280 --> 00:06:19.780
If the 2% requirement were put in place today,
you would still have Joe Biden, Bernie Sanders,

00:06:19.780 --> 00:06:26.040
Elizabeth Warren, Kamala Harris, Pete Buddha,
judge Beto O'rourke and Cory booker.

00:06:26.040 --> 00:06:27.560
That's seven candidates.

00:06:27.560 --> 00:06:28.560
Okay.

00:06:28.560 --> 00:06:33.470
If we have seven candidates by the third debate,
it is very reasonable.

00:06:33.470 --> 00:06:41.210
And again, if you participate in to national
debates and you can't get 2% I don't believe

00:06:41.210 --> 00:06:46.180
you deserve to keep taking up space on the
stage, you don't have a shot.

00:06:46.180 --> 00:06:49.650
So the only debate for me is about the individual
donor number.

00:06:49.650 --> 00:06:57.360
I get that donations are a way to prove your
viability, but 130,000 donors at 14 months

00:06:57.360 --> 00:07:02.060
before the election, which is effectively
what September will be.

00:07:02.060 --> 00:07:03.280
That might be too high.

00:07:03.280 --> 00:07:04.280
Okay.

00:07:04.280 --> 00:07:08.990
Can somebody pulling 1.8% in October end up
being the nominee by June?

00:07:08.990 --> 00:07:10.530
I don't think they can.

00:07:10.530 --> 00:07:15.920
Can someone with only 100,000 donors in octo
in October end up being the nominee in June?

00:07:15.920 --> 00:07:16.920
I think they can.

00:07:16.920 --> 00:07:20.330
I mean, it may be a long shot compared to
some of the other candidates, but that's where

00:07:20.330 --> 00:07:23.710
the focus should be on getting these requirements
changed.

00:07:23.710 --> 00:07:29.410
1% to be in debates, one to 2% to be in debates
three and four completely reasonable.

00:07:29.410 --> 00:07:34.840
And I have not seen any serious argument,
uh, that that is too high of a requirement.

00:07:34.840 --> 00:07:36.550
If you think I'm wrong, let me know.

